{"name":"Capri Water Blue","hex":"#abe2d6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"capri","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep shade of sky blue between cyan and azure.","Used in capri pants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/capri"},{"term":"water","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An inorganic compound (of molecular formula .mw-parser-output .template-chem2-su{display:inline-block;font-size:80%;line-height:1;vertical-align:-0.35em}.mw-parser-output .template-chem2-su>span{display:block;text-align:left}.mw-parser-output sub.template-chem2-sub{font-size:80%;vertical-align:-0.35em}.mw-parser-output sup.template-chem2-sup{font-size:80%;vertical-align:0.65em}H2O) found at room temperature and pressure as a clear liquid; it is present naturally as rain, and found in rivers, lakes and seas; its solid form is ice and its gaseous form is steam.","The liquid form of this substance: liquid H2O."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To wet or supply with water; to moisten; to overflow with water; to irrigate.\n\n  To pour water into the soil surrounding (plants).\n\n  To provide (animals) with water for drinking.","To pour water into the soil surrounding (plants)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/water"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Water blue","blocks":[{"text":"Water blue, also known as aniline blue, Acid blue 22, Soluble Blue 3M, Marine Blue V, or C.I. 42755, is a chemical compound used as a stain in histology. Water supply blue stains collagen blue in tissue sections. It is soluble in water and slightly soluble in ethanol."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Water_blue2.png/330px-Water_blue2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Water_blue","wikidata":"Q421881"},{"title":"Capri","blocks":[{"text":"Capri is an island located in the Tyrrhenian Sea off the Sorrento Peninsula, on the south side of the Gulf of Naples in the Campania region of Italy. A resort destination since the time of the Roman Republic, it is known for its natural beauty, historic sites, and tourism industry. It has 13,451 inhabitants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Capri_in_Cartolina_-_Vista_da_Termini_%28Massa_Lubrense%29.jpg/330px-Capri_in_Cartolina_-_Vista_da_Termini_%28Massa_Lubrense%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capri","wikidata":"Q173292"},{"title":"Water","blocks":[{"text":"Water is an inorganic compound with the chemical formula H2O. It is a transparent, tasteless, odorless, and nearly colorless chemical substance. It is the main constituent of Earth's streams, lakes, and oceans. Water is also the fluid of all known living organisms, in which it acts as a solvent. Water, being a polar molecule, undergoes strong intermolecular hydrogen bonding which is a large contributor to its physical and chemical properties. It is vital for all known forms of life, despite not providing food energy or being an organic micronutrient. Due to its presence in all organisms, its chemical stability, its worldwide abundance, and its strong polarity relative to its small molecular size, water is often referred to as the \"universal solvent\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/H2O_2D_labelled.svg/330px-H2O_2D_labelled.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Water","wikidata":"Q283"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/%D0%9A%D0%B0%D0%BF%D1%80%D0%B8_%D0%A0%D1%83%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%8B_%D0%92%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%BB%D1%8B_%D0%AE%D0%BF%D0%B8%D1%82%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B0.jpg/500px-%D0%9A%D0%B0%D0%BF%D1%80%D0%B8_%D0%A0%D1%83%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%8B_%D0%92%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%BB%D1%8B_%D0%AE%D0%BF%D0%B8%D1%82%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/%D0%9A%D0%B0%D0%BF%D1%80%D0%B8_%D0%A0%D1%83%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%8B_%D0%92%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%BB%D1%8B_%D0%AE%D0%BF%D0%B8%D1%82%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B0.jpg/1280px-%D0%9A%D0%B0%D0%BF%D1%80%D0%B8_%D0%A0%D1%83%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%8B_%D0%92%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%BB%D1%8B_%D0%AE%D0%BF%D0%B8%D1%82%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/%D0%9A%D0%B0%D0%BF%D1%80%D0%B8_%D0%A0%D1%83%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%8B_%D0%92%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%BB%D1%8B_%D0%AE%D0%BF%D0%B8%D1%82